# Test: a reload deleting a live mirror target is refused and the kernel mirror stays
#
# VALIDATES: AC-2 on a real kernel. The running config mirrors the ingress of
#            zmtsrc0 to zmtdst0, a veth pair the driver creates. A SIGHUP whose
#            config deletes the zmtdst0 entry while the mirror still names it is
#            refused, naming the mirror leaf and the deleted name, and the traffic control
#            mirred filter on zmtsrc0 still copies to zmtdst0 afterwards. A
#            second SIGHUP that removes the mirror and the target together
#            completes, and zmtsrc0 then holds no tc filter on either clsact
#            hook.
# PREVENTS: a reload deleting a mirror target committing with the mirror left
#           pointing at nothing, a refused reload that still disturbed the live
#           mirror, and an ordered removal that left the tc filter behind.
#
# Question: is the deletion of a target the live kernel mirror uses refused
# while that mirror survives, and does removing both retire it? A unit test
# cannot decide it: the refusal is the daemon's reload validation, and the
# evidence is the tc filter state the kernel backend installed.
#
# Method: one foreground driver (internal/test/fixture/iface_mirror_fixture_linux.go)
# creates the veth pair and starts its own daemon, because it must read each
# reload's outcome line before it sends the next one. It reads the source's
# clsact hooks over netlink after each outcome line, so no step waits on a
# timer, and it deletes the pair at the end.

# needs-linux: traffic control and veth exist only on Linux. caps=net-admin: the driver and
# the daemon create links and program tc filters.
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture reload/tx-iface-mirror-target-delete-refused:timeout=90s

expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=MIRROR-INSTALLED zmtsrc0 zmtdst0
expect=stderr:contains=interface/ethernet[zmtsrc0]/unit[0]/mirror/ingress
expect=stderr:contains=interface "zmtdst0" is not configured
expect=stdout:contains=MIRROR-KEPT-AFTER-REFUSAL zmtsrc0 zmtdst0
expect=stderr:contains=sighup reload complete
expect=stdout:contains=MIRROR-RETIRED zmtsrc0
